// A kernel that requires blocks of 1,024 threads (.reqntid: Triton writes it for every kernel), in
// which a V100 allows 64 registers a thread. ptxas gives it 64 for sm_75: 56 values that each thread
// keeps through a loop (read from the zeroed output, so that they are not constants), and two uniform
// registers for the arithmetic of the loop, which comes from the block's indices alone. The usual
// translation puts the uniform registers above the program's: 66 registers, and a V100 allows blocks
// of 896 threads at most. A program that reads that limit before it launches (Triton) stops there,
// and a launch of 1,024 threads is refused. The layer translates it within 64 instead (the uniform
// registers in the thread's local memory: tests/gpu/run.sh, `cubin-required-block-within`).
// Every thread stores the same four words: the exclusive or, the sum and a weighted sum of the 56
// values after `rounds` rounds, and `rounds`.
//   toolkits/cuda-13.5.0/bin/ptxas -arch=sm_75 -lineinfo -o k_required_block_within.sm75.cubin k_required_block_within.ptx
